{"name":"Atlantic Breeze","hex":"#cbe1ee","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"atlantic","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of or pertaining to the atlas, the uppermost vertebra in the spinal columns of humans and some other animals."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/atlantic"},{"term":"breeze","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A light, gentle wind.","Any activity that is easy, not testing or difficult."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To move casually, in a carefree manner.","To blow gently."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/breeze"}],"entries":[{"title":"Breeze (rapper)","blocks":[{"text":"Morgan Rodriguez, professionally known by his stage name MC Breeze, is an American rapper from Los Angeles. He released his only studio album, T.Y.S.O.N. , in 1989 via Atlantic Records. The album, which was produced by the L.A. Posse, made it to number 60 on the US Billboard Top R&B/Hip-Hop Albums. The record spawned two singles: \"Great Big Freak\" and \"L.A. Posse\". The latter peaked at No. 79 on the US Hot R&B/Hip-Hop Songs, No. 8 on the US Hot Rap Songs, and later was ranked at No. 64 by Complex's list of The 100 Best L.A. Rap Songs."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Breeze_(rapper)","wikidata":"Q17108589"},{"title":"Atlantic Ocean","blocks":[{"text":"The Atlantic Ocean is the second largest of the world's five oceans, with an area of about 85,133,000 square kilometers (32,870,000 sq mi). It covers approximately 17% of Earth's surface and about 24% of its water surface area. During the Age of Discovery, it was known for separating the New World of the Americas from the Old World of Afro-Eurasia."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/4/47/Atlantic_Ocean_-_en.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Atlantic_Ocean","wikidata":"Q97"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedi